claim.claim-text:
1. In a method performed by a base station in the wireless communication system, a method comprising:
A step to transmit codebooks allocated for data transmission to each of multiple user terminals;
A step to receive the pilot and the data from one or more user terminals among the multiple user terminals;
A step to generate the active user information based on the above-mentioned data;
A step to detect active user terminals among the above-mentioned multiple user terminals based on the above-mentioned pilot and active user information;
A step to generate the channel estimation information related to the above-mentioned active user terminals; and
A step to detect the data of the active user terminal based on the above-mentioned channel estimation information.

6. In a method performed by user terminals in the wireless communication system, a method comprising:
A step to receive a codebook allocated for the data transmission of the above-mentioned user terminal from a base station;
A step to generate the data based on the above-mentioned codebook;
A step to select or create a pilot; and
A step to transmit the above-mentioned pilot and data to the above-mentioned base station,
Wherein the above-mentioned user terminal is detected as an active user terminal among multiple user terminals based on the above-mentioned pilot and the active user information generated based on the above-mentioned data.

9. The method of claim 6,
Wherein the above-mentioned user terminal is detected as the active user terminal among the above-mentioned multiple user terminals based on a learned neural network;
Wherein the above-mentioned neural network is learned based on the step 1 learning and the step 2 learning;
Wherein the above-mentioned step 1 learning is performed using a first loss function defined based on the information indicating the activation states of the above-mentioned multiple user terminals and the above-mentioned active user information; and
Wherein the above-mentioned step 2 learning is performed using a second loss function defined based on the information indicating activation states of the above-mentioned multiple user terminals and the information indicating the estimated activation states for the above-mentioned multiple user terminals.
